-- TRIEL example inside the formal core: purpose limitation as a gate on the
-- actions of an AI agent. The agent may transfer personal data for a new
-- purpose only when the new purpose is compatible with the purpose for which
-- the data were collected, after Articles 5(1)(b) and 8A of the UK GDPR: a
-- permission and a prohibition with complementary conditions, a breach
-- handler bound to the prohibition, and an invariant.
--
-- This is a stylised reading of Article 8A, not a formalisation of it. The
-- example keeps three routes by which a new purpose counts as compatible: the
-- data subject has consented to the processing for the new purpose
-- (new_purpose_consented); the processing meets a condition in Annex 2
-- (annex2_condition_met); or the controller has assessed the new purpose as
-- compatible, taking into account the matters listed in Article 8A(2)
-- (assessed_compatible). Article 8A(4) is omitted, and so is every other part
-- of the article.
--
-- The rule is written by the controller, and so are its data. TRIEL does not
-- decide which purposes are compatible: whether the data subject consented,
-- whether an Annex 2 condition is met and how the matters of Article 8A(2)
-- weigh are determinations of the controller, which it records as the three
-- factors. The specification only checks the transfers of the agent against
-- what is on record. The three factors come from the controller, declared an
-- ORACLE, so PROVENANCE_REQUIRED is true (formal/core/CORE.md, section 9,
-- decision 28); without it the translator rejects the specification ("ORACLE
-- source without PROVENANCE_REQUIRED"). The fact that data were transferred
-- is reported by the agent itself.
--
-- A consent is fresh for 30 days after it arrives and an assessment for 90
-- days (MAX_AGE ... ON_STALE BLOCK); the two periods are assumptions of this
-- example, not periods of the article. A factor that is older, or present at
-- activation without an arrival, is absent (examples/core/README.md,
-- conventions 3 and 4). The Annex 2 condition has no MAX_AGE.
--
-- Both conditions are read in the state of the entry just before the
-- transfer. If one of the three factors is true there, the permission is
-- exercised (FULFILLED) and the monitor of the prohibition lets the transfer
-- through (purpose_consented). If all three are false, the prohibition is
-- breached at the transfer, the handler notifies the reviewer, and the
-- monitor blocks it (purpose_no_route). If none is true and one is absent,
-- because it is not on record or is stale, both conditions are undefined: the
-- permission is not exercised and the prohibition is not breached, and the
-- fail-closed monitor blocks the transfer, since its condition is not known
-- to be false (purpose_not_on_record, purpose_stale_assessment;
-- undefined_guard_blocks_not_breach).
--
-- The invariant reads data_transferred in the state of the entry of the
-- transfer. It is F from an entry where data were transferred and none of
-- the three routes is true; ALWAYS is never T on a finite trace
-- (always_never_true), so otherwise it is U. The invariant reports, it does
-- not block. Every construct in this file is translated into the Isabelle/HOL
-- core (formal/core) and evaluated by the exported evaluator (evaluator/).

SPECIFICATION purpose_limitation_gate VERSION 1.0.0
    JURISDICTION "UK"
    PROVENANCE_REQUIRED: true

SUBJECTS {
  agent      : PARTY,
  controller : ORACLE,
  reviewer   : REGULATOR
}

TERMS {
  agent MAY transfer_personal_data
    WHEN new_purpose_consented OR annex2_condition_met OR assessed_compatible;
  agent MUST_NOT transfer_personal_data
    WHEN NOT (new_purpose_consented OR annex2_condition_met OR assessed_compatible);
  agent ON_BREACH NOTIFY reviewer
}

FACTORS {
  new_purpose_consented : Boolean METADATA SOURCE controller
                          MAX_AGE 30 DAYS ON_STALE BLOCK,
  annex2_condition_met  : Boolean METADATA SOURCE controller,
  assessed_compatible   : Boolean METADATA SOURCE controller
                          MAX_AGE 90 DAYS ON_STALE BLOCK,
  data_transferred      : Boolean METADATA SOURCE agent
}

INVARIANTS {
  compatible_transfers_only : SAFETY :
    ALWAYS(data_transferred IMPLIES
           (new_purpose_consented OR annex2_condition_met OR assessed_compatible))
}
